# built-site.xyz turned 90 deg about the centre of its ground patch, then
# translated (6, -4, 0). GROUND TRUTH mis-alignment for the built-scene E2E test.
#
# 90 deg rather than a smaller angle for two reasons: it is far outside the
# +/-30 deg window a scanner-heading prior would clamp the coarse search to (so
# this pair fails loudly if that prior is ever applied ungated again), and a
# quarter turn about the centre of a SQUARE footprint leaves the bounding box
# unchanged -- which is what makes the bounds assertion in the spec meaningful.
